      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name changed from Deuce of Hearts to New Home as the community grew in the early twentieth century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/new-home-tx-lynn-county",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Cotton has driven New Home’s economy since the 1900s, with the local gin processing 12,000 bales in 1985.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Home%2C_Texas",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "New Home sits on the high plains of the Llano Estacado, a vast flatland that defines much of West Texas.",
